{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "trail-race-app-collection-v2",
    "name": "Trail Race App",
    "description": "Full API collection for the Trail Race CQRS backend.\n\n## Quick Start\n1. Import this file into Postman (File → Import)\n2. Run **Login as Administrator** first — `jwt_token` is set automatically\n3. All other requests inherit the Bearer token from the collection auth\n\n## Seed Credentials\n| Email | Password | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| admin@trailrace.com | admin123 | ADMINISTRATOR |\n| jane@example.com | applicant123 | APPLICANT |\n| marco@example.com | applicant123 | APPLICANT |\n| lena@example.com | applicant123 | APPLICANT |\n\n## Seed Races\n6 sample races are pre-loaded: Mountain Trail 5K, Forest Loop 10K, Coastal Half Marathon, Alpine Marathon, City Park 5K, River Valley 10K.\n\n## Base URLs (configurable via variables)\n- Command Service: `http://localhost:8081`\n- Query Service: `http://localhost:8082`\n\n## Recommended Execution Order\n1. Health checks → 2. Login → 3. Create Race → 4. Create Application → 5. Query reads → 6. Update → 7. Error scenarios → 8. Delete\n\n> **CQRS note:** After a write (command service), the query service may take a few hundred milliseconds to process the RabbitMQ event. If a GET returns stale data, wait briefly and retry.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "command_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "description": "Command service base URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "query_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8082",
      "description": "Query service base URL"
    },
    {
      "key": "jwt_token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-populated after running a Login request"
    },
    {
      "key": "jwt_token_applicant",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-populated after Login as Applicant"
    },
    {
      "key": "race_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-populated after creating a race"
    },
    {
      "key": "application_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-populated after creating an application"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{jwt_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health & Info",
      "description": "Unauthenticated health and info endpoints. Run these first to verify both services are up.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health — Command Service",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Service is UP', function () {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('DB component is UP', function () {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.components.db.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('RabbitMQ component is UP', function () {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.components.rabbit.status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{command_url}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{command_url}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Returns health status of the command service including DB and RabbitMQ components. No auth required."
          },
          "response": [
